1
00:01:13,680 --> 00:01:15,079
Come on.

2
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:19,359
There's nothing here. It's empty.
Where's the shipment?

3
00:02:33,320 --> 00:02:36,153
Joey, Joey, Joey,
all you gotta do is knock, huh?

4
00:02:36,320 --> 00:02:37,548
All right, who tipped you?

5
00:02:37,720 --> 00:02:40,109
- Don't know what you're talking about.
- Come on, who was it?

6
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:41,998
Just because
you made a little mistake here,

7
00:02:42,160 --> 00:02:44,469
let's not get paranoid, Joey.

8
00:02:44,640 --> 00:02:47,438
You call me Joey one more time,
I'm gonna make you eat this flashlight.

9
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:49,431
- Take it easy.
- I ought to--

10
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:50,589
I'd give up my pension

11
00:02:50,760 --> 00:02:52,352
for just five minutes alone
with this guy.

12
00:02:52,520 --> 00:02:53,555
Two minutes is all I need.

13
00:02:53,720 --> 00:02:54,948
- Hey, come on.
- Joe, stop.

14
00:02:55,120 --> 00:02:57,793
- Come on, get real.
- Joe!

15
00:02:57,960 --> 00:02:59,552
- For you, I'll use my bare hands.
- Hey.

16
00:03:00,920 --> 00:03:02,433
- Come here.
- Hold on.

17
00:03:02,600 --> 00:03:05,353
All right, it's all right.
Everything's all right, under control.

18
00:03:05,520 --> 00:03:08,080
Your bosses are gonna hear
that you muscled me, I promise you.

19
00:03:08,240 --> 00:03:09,593
No, you're gonna hear from me too.

20
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:14,153
You just cut the tag off your mattress,
I'm gonna be right in your face.

21
00:03:14,320 --> 00:03:17,790
It's all right, I'm all right.
All right there.

22
00:03:17,960 --> 00:03:22,476
See, you can fix a lot of things, Harry,
but I'm one thing you can't fix, huh?

23
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:25,589
Let's go. Come on.

24
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:36,436
<i>WATB sending</i>
<i>groovy sounds your way</i>

25
00:03:36,600 --> 00:03:38,670
<i>at 8/32</i>
<i>on this cloudy Atlanta morning.</i>

26
00:03:38,840 --> 00:03:41,035
<i>But it looks like the rain is over</i>
<i>for now.</i>

27
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:42,315
<i>Temperature downtown at the--</i>

28
00:03:42,480 --> 00:03:45,677
- Yeah, so?
- So I'll see you.

29
00:03:45,840 --> 00:03:47,671
See you later.

30
00:04:39,280 --> 00:04:43,432
There you are.
I've been looking all over for you.

31
00:04:46,480 --> 00:04:47,515
What happened to you?

32
00:04:47,680 --> 00:04:51,309
- I cut myself shaving.
- With a machete?

33
00:04:51,480 --> 00:04:54,074
- I got mugged.
- Get out of here.

34
00:04:55,120 --> 00:04:57,236
You got mugged?

35
00:04:58,040 --> 00:05:00,713
- Did you find them?
- No, not yet.

36
00:05:00,880 --> 00:05:01,995
But Harry Landers sent them.

37
00:05:02,160 --> 00:05:04,037
- You can be sure of that.
- Harry La--?

38
00:05:04,200 --> 00:05:05,997
You got Harry Landers on the brain,
you know.

39
00:05:06,160 --> 00:05:09,675
This is no ordinary mugging.
They took my badge and my gun.

40
00:05:10,480 --> 00:05:13,677
Okay. Okay.

41
00:05:13,840 --> 00:05:16,957
Look, Joe, go home,
cool off, all right?

42
00:05:17,120 --> 00:05:18,997
I'll cover for you.

43
00:05:19,160 --> 00:05:21,435
That's a good idea.
I got some things to do.

44
00:05:21,600 --> 00:05:24,034
Joe. Joe, don't.

45
00:05:24,200 --> 00:05:27,078
Look, I grabbed one of the guys.
I ripped his pocket.

46
00:05:27,240 --> 00:05:30,073
Found a laundry slip
from an all-night joint on 1 1th.

47
00:05:30,240 --> 00:05:31,992
I'm gonna go back there,
recognise those guys.

48
00:05:32,160 --> 00:05:35,311
- I'm gonna nail them.
- Joe, don't go crazy.

49
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:38,711
I gotta get my badge and my gun back,
find those punks,

50
00:05:38,880 --> 00:05:40,836
and then I'm gonna
balance the books with Harry.

51
00:05:43,120 --> 00:05:44,917
May I?

52
00:05:58,840 --> 00:06:00,717
You just bring the goods
to Freddie's place

53
00:06:00,880 --> 00:06:02,757
and I'll take delivery there.

54
00:06:02,920 --> 00:06:05,798
Everything else
is the same as always.

55
00:06:07,360 --> 00:06:09,749
No, nothing, nothing.
I've just got a little heat on me.

56
00:06:09,920 --> 00:06:12,878
It's merely a temporary thing,
believe me.

57
00:06:17,640 --> 00:06:22,156
All right. I'll expect to hear from you.

58
00:06:24,600 --> 00:06:26,079
What are you doing here?

59
00:06:58,840 --> 00:07:00,796
Harry Landers?

60
00:07:08,080 --> 00:07:09,479
Michael.

61
00:07:11,280 --> 00:07:13,840
Just got the call, captain.

62
00:07:19,800 --> 00:07:21,950
Where's Joe Peters?

63
00:07:22,120 --> 00:07:24,714
We were on surveillance

64
00:07:24,880 --> 00:07:27,678
and the suspects split up,
so we had to follow them separately.

65
00:07:27,840 --> 00:07:30,035
So you don't know where he is,
do you?

66
00:07:31,680 --> 00:07:34,353
No, sir, not at the moment, no.

67
00:07:34,520 --> 00:07:39,275
Michael,
you've a long career ahead of you.

68
00:07:39,440 --> 00:07:42,477
Don't you let one rotten apple
spoil it for you, you hear?

69
00:07:43,160 --> 00:07:45,674
I don't know what you mean, sir.

70
00:07:45,840 --> 00:07:48,673
I want you to tell me the truth,
Michael.

71
00:07:48,840 --> 00:07:51,559
Did Joe Peters do this?

72
00:07:54,920 --> 00:07:57,150
It's a beauty, Roy. Runs like a top.

73
00:07:57,320 --> 00:08:00,153
This truck will take any hill in Georgia
in high gear.

74
00:08:00,320 --> 00:08:01,435
How'd you come by it?

75
00:08:01,600 --> 00:08:03,670
- Did you know George Gibson?
- No.

76
00:08:03,840 --> 00:08:06,229
Well, I helped George make out his will
just before he died.

77
00:08:06,400 --> 00:08:09,278
- And he paid you with the truck.
- Paid me with the truck.

78
00:08:09,440 --> 00:08:11,749
How much you want for it?

79
00:08:12,720 --> 00:08:14,392
Five hundred dollars.

80
00:08:14,560 --> 00:08:17,028
Well, look at the tyres
and the shape it's in.

81
00:08:17,200 --> 00:08:20,431
- But it needs paint.
- Well, just a few places.

82
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:22,989
Listen to this. This is the heart of it.

83
00:08:29,440 --> 00:08:31,192
Sounds like a Budapest symphony.

84
00:08:34,720 --> 00:08:36,915
- How much did you say?
- Five hundred.

85
00:08:37,080 --> 00:08:40,390
- I'll give you 300.
- I'll take 4 75.

86
00:08:40,560 --> 00:08:42,710
- Three twenty-five.
- Four sixty.

87
00:08:42,880 --> 00:08:44,233
- Three fifty.
- Four fifty.

88
00:08:44,400 --> 00:08:46,516
- Three seventy-five.
- I'll tell you what.

89
00:08:46,680 --> 00:08:49,717
Take it home,
have Estelle drive it a couple of weeks.

90
00:08:49,880 --> 00:08:51,950
If she likes it, give me 400.

91
00:08:52,120 --> 00:08:54,395
If she doesn't,
just have her park it out back.

92
00:08:54,560 --> 00:08:57,836
Tell Estelle happy birthday
and drive it in good health.

93
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:00,912
- Well, Joe, off today, huh?
- Hi, Ben.

94
00:09:01,080 --> 00:09:03,230
- Your office said you'd be here.
- Oh, yeah, yeah.

95
00:09:03,400 --> 00:09:05,994
A lot of stuff to do around here.

96
00:09:07,240 --> 00:09:10,630
It'll stop that as soon as it warms up.

97
00:09:11,800 --> 00:09:15,110
- I've gotta talk to you.
- Let's walk along.

98
00:09:16,560 --> 00:09:19,028
You heard about Harry Landers?
He was the biggest fence around,

99
00:09:19,200 --> 00:09:21,031
and he always knew
when a bust was going down.

100
00:09:21,200 --> 00:09:25,273
- Well, somebody was tipping him off.
- You don't say.

101
00:09:25,440 --> 00:09:28,876
I think Landers was iced
by somebody in the department,

102
00:09:29,040 --> 00:09:30,792
the same guy he was paying off.

103
00:09:31,960 --> 00:09:34,599
Joe Peters is guilty.
There's no doubt about it.

104
00:09:34,760 --> 00:09:38,275
Joe Peters is a lot of things,
but dirty he's not.

105
00:09:40,200 --> 00:09:41,838
We've got his gun.

106
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:43,115
The boys found it in a sewer

107
00:09:43,280 --> 00:09:44,952
a couple of blocks
from Landers' warehouse,

108
00:09:45,120 --> 00:09:46,314
where he tossed it afterwards.

109
00:09:46,480 --> 00:09:49,790
And Ballistics says it's the same bullet
they dug out of Harry Landers.

110
00:09:49,960 --> 00:09:53,270
And we've got an eyewitness
that puts him at the scene.

111
00:09:54,520 --> 00:09:55,873
I thought he had an alibi.

112
00:09:57,040 --> 00:09:58,155
So did he.

113
00:09:58,320 --> 00:10:00,436
My partner tried to cover for me,
but it's--

114
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:02,670
It's not gonna scan.

115
00:10:04,160 --> 00:10:06,515
- Have you got a knife?
- Landers was shot.

116
00:10:06,680 --> 00:10:09,353
I mean to open this sack of feed.

117
00:10:10,240 --> 00:10:12,959
- Internal Affairs is on the case.
- Thank you.

118
00:10:13,120 --> 00:10:16,237
Yeah, they like me
for taking out Landers.

119
00:10:16,400 --> 00:10:19,278
I was staking out a cleaning joint,
looking for the guys who mugged me

120
00:10:19,440 --> 00:10:20,668
when Landers was killed,

121
00:10:20,840 --> 00:10:22,592
but I can't substantiate
that I was there.

122
00:10:22,760 --> 00:10:26,355
- Here, chick, chick, chick.
- My gun was found near the scene.

123
00:10:26,520 --> 00:10:27,873
Here, chick, chick, chick.

124
00:10:28,320 --> 00:10:30,834
Those clowns who took it
were working for whoever set me up.

125
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:34,197
- Peters was on Landers' payroll.
- Well, it doesn't make any sense.

126
00:10:34,360 --> 00:10:36,954
If he was on his payroll,
why would he kill him?

127
00:10:37,120 --> 00:10:39,190
- What are you, his lawyer?
- No, I'm not his lawyer.

128
00:10:39,360 --> 00:10:41,794
The man was a cop, my cop,
and I wanna know what kind of case

129
00:10:41,960 --> 00:10:44,633
you got against him before I run out
and charge him with murder.

130
00:10:45,960 --> 00:10:48,520
This is a copy of his bank statement.

131
00:10:48,680 --> 00:10:51,194
You'll notice
a deposit was made ten days ago.

132
00:10:51,360 --> 00:10:52,873
Fifty thousand dollars.

133
00:10:55,960 --> 00:10:57,791
And you're saying
this is bribe money?

134
00:10:57,960 --> 00:11:00,030
Well, he didn't get it
from the tooth fairy.

135
00:11:00,200 --> 00:11:01,758
Get. Get out of here.

136
00:11:01,920 --> 00:11:04,957
That banty rooster's got his eye
on that Rhode Island Red hen.

137
00:11:05,120 --> 00:11:06,712
Every time
that big rooster comes around,

138
00:11:06,880 --> 00:11:08,279
he wants to fight.

139
00:11:08,440 --> 00:11:10,078
Kind of silly, isn't it?

140
00:11:10,720 --> 00:11:12,438
Well, you gonna take my case
or not?

141
00:11:13,320 --> 00:11:15,709
The last time I saw you
was in a courtroom.

142
00:11:15,880 --> 00:11:18,553
You were trying to railroad my client
Mr. James Plesko,

143
00:11:18,720 --> 00:11:20,438
into the penitentiary.

144
00:11:20,600 --> 00:11:24,195
Seems like you're about to get
the same deal you gave Mr. Plesko.

145
00:11:24,360 --> 00:11:28,194
I was just doing my job.
And who's to say he didn't do it?

146
00:11:28,360 --> 00:11:30,510
The jury found him innocent.

147
00:11:31,040 --> 00:11:33,031
All right,
if you're not gonna take my case,

148
00:11:33,200 --> 00:11:35,191
why didn't you just say so
to begin with?

149
00:11:35,360 --> 00:11:38,113
I didn't say I wouldn't take your case.

150
00:11:38,720 --> 00:11:43,271
Just seems kind of poetic,
the turn of circumstances here.

151
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:45,715
Ben, this is my neck.

152
00:11:45,880 --> 00:11:49,350
Those guys don't like me to begin with.
I mean, they're gonna nail me.

153
00:11:49,520 --> 00:11:53,354
Ben, I need you.
Now, what's it gonna be?

154
00:11:53,520 --> 00:11:56,751
Well, if I'm going into town,
I've got to go in the house and change.

155
00:11:57,480 --> 00:12:00,472
You're not the smartest cop I ever saw,
but I don't think you're dumb enough

156
00:12:00,640 --> 00:12:03,552
to kill this fellow
and concoct a story like this one.

157
00:12:03,720 --> 00:12:06,951
Ben, I didn't do it.

158
00:12:07,640 --> 00:12:09,835
That's just what Mr. Plesko said.

159
00:12:23,520 --> 00:12:25,397
- Hey, the door's opening.
- Hey, here he comes.

160
00:12:25,560 --> 00:12:26,834
- Joe, Joe, why did you--?
- Joe?

161
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:28,433
- Hold it.
- Joe? Joe?

162
00:12:28,600 --> 00:12:33,958
- Hold it, hold it, hold it!
- Joe.

163
00:12:34,560 --> 00:12:38,235
It's true Joe Peters
has been disciplined for using force.

164
00:12:38,400 --> 00:12:40,118
But he has three citations for valour

165
00:12:40,280 --> 00:12:42,430
and a commendation
from the mayor's office.

166
00:12:42,600 --> 00:12:46,912
He's been hospitalized five times
for injuries received in the line of duty.

167
00:12:47,080 --> 00:12:48,672
Joe Peters is innocent

168
00:12:48,840 --> 00:12:51,912
and expects to be vindicated
by the court.

169
00:12:52,840 --> 00:12:54,114
- Hold it.
- What about the--?

170
00:12:54,280 --> 00:12:58,353
Hold it, hold it, hold it!

171
00:12:58,520 --> 00:13:01,876
- That's all.
- Oh, but what about--?

172
00:13:02,040 --> 00:13:05,237
- Come on.
- Give me a break.

173
00:13:35,360 --> 00:13:39,114
- What say, Tyler?
- Not much.

174
00:13:39,280 --> 00:13:42,272
There's dozens of prints in there,
but they're all smudged.

175
00:13:42,440 --> 00:13:44,237
Landers' .357 Magnum's
in the desk drawer.

176
00:13:44,400 --> 00:13:47,392
- Hadn't been fired.
- You know Joe Peters?

177
00:13:48,400 --> 00:13:51,551
- We've met.
- Where was the body?

178
00:13:52,720 --> 00:13:55,075
Over here in this little office.

179
00:13:55,240 --> 00:13:56,673
Now, whoever pulled the trigger

180
00:13:56,840 --> 00:13:58,671
was standing
directly across the desk from him

181
00:13:58,840 --> 00:14:01,149
when they fired the shot.

182
00:14:02,480 --> 00:14:04,994
- Thank you, Mr. Coyle.
- You're welcome.

183
00:14:09,080 --> 00:14:10,433
What's his story?

184
00:14:10,600 --> 00:14:13,637
He's the eyewitness
who says he saw you running away.

185
00:14:13,800 --> 00:14:16,678
- He's lying.
- No.

186
00:14:17,520 --> 00:14:19,875
You don't talk to or touch anybody.

187
00:14:20,040 --> 00:14:22,508
If you get any bright ideas,
check them with me.

188
00:14:22,680 --> 00:14:26,275
- Say hello to my daughter Charlene.
- How do you do?

189
00:14:32,880 --> 00:14:34,552
All right, so, what do we do?

190
00:14:34,720 --> 00:14:36,950
Well, I'd say,

191
00:14:37,120 --> 00:14:39,998
let's try to find those fellows
who took your gun and badge.

192
00:14:40,160 --> 00:14:42,549
I'll stake out that laundry.
They'll be back sooner or later.

193
00:14:42,720 --> 00:14:43,789
Tyler, you go with him.

194
00:14:43,960 --> 00:14:47,111
If he sees them, you make contact.
You just look and point.

195
00:14:47,280 --> 00:14:48,998
Do I make myself clear?

196
00:14:49,560 --> 00:14:50,629
Absolutely.

197
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:54,272
Let's go.

198
00:14:55,800 --> 00:14:58,189
You're sending me on a stakeout
with Dirty Harry?

199
00:14:58,360 --> 00:15:01,079
Somebody has to do it,
and I'm too old.

200
00:15:05,560 --> 00:15:07,312
Shall I have a talk with his partner,
Danello?

201
00:15:07,880 --> 00:15:10,075
Yeah. I'll be at the department.

202
00:15:10,240 --> 00:15:13,277
See if anybody down there
remembers my name.

203
00:15:22,560 --> 00:15:24,551
- Morning, gentlemen.
- Ben.

204
00:15:24,720 --> 00:15:27,314
- You here on the Peters case?
- Yeah.

205
00:15:28,840 --> 00:15:30,637
Good luck.

206
00:15:35,040 --> 00:15:36,234
Well, what'd you expect, Ben?

207
00:15:38,040 --> 00:15:41,396
I was hoping maybe Joe Peters
had a friend or two.

208
00:15:41,560 --> 00:15:44,438
Joe Peters is not a very popular man
around here nowadays, Ben.

209
00:15:44,600 --> 00:15:46,318
What about you?

210
00:15:46,480 --> 00:15:49,995
Well, I'll say this for him:
He was a hard charger.

211
00:15:50,600 --> 00:15:52,192
But he also had
the lowest conviction rate

212
00:15:52,360 --> 00:15:53,349
on my squad.

213
00:15:53,520 --> 00:15:56,512
The guy would charge out half-cocked.
Bad warrants, insufficient evidence.

214
00:15:56,680 --> 00:15:59,148
Well, what happens
to the Harry Landers investigation

215
00:15:59,320 --> 00:16:00,389
if he goes to prison?

216
00:16:00,560 --> 00:16:02,915
I don't know, maybe we'll do better.

217
00:16:03,080 --> 00:16:05,753
Are you saying
you think Joe was on his payroll?

218
00:16:05,920 --> 00:16:09,390
Well, how would you explain 50 grand
in his bank account?

219
00:16:10,040 --> 00:16:11,678
Anybody could've
deposited that money

220
00:16:11,840 --> 00:16:13,478
without Joe's knowledge.

221
00:16:13,640 --> 00:16:16,359
Fifty thousand dollars?

222
00:16:16,520 --> 00:16:18,715
That's a drop in the bucket
to a big operation.

223
00:16:18,880 --> 00:16:20,108
Besides, if he was paying him,

224
00:16:20,280 --> 00:16:22,157
why kill the goose
that laid the golden egg?

225
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:24,390
I don't know.

226
00:16:24,560 --> 00:16:27,757
I sure would like to take a look
at the Harry Landers file.

227
00:16:27,920 --> 00:16:29,672
Now, come on, Ben.
You know I can't do that.

228
00:16:29,840 --> 00:16:32,912
The files are confidential.
It's an ongoing investigation.

229
00:16:33,080 --> 00:16:35,116
I can make a discovery motion.

230
00:16:35,280 --> 00:16:38,670
Well, if you do, you'll have to come
back to me with the judge's signature.

231
00:16:38,840 --> 00:16:40,751
You know that.

232
00:16:42,160 --> 00:16:44,515
Let me ask you this.

233
00:16:44,680 --> 00:16:47,148
How long do you think Joe will last
in prison?

234
00:16:48,600 --> 00:16:50,955
I don't know. It's out of my hands.

235
00:16:52,120 --> 00:16:57,069
Yeah. I guess it is. See you, Frank.

236
00:17:03,640 --> 00:17:05,710
Tony, another round
for the boys here.

237
00:17:05,880 --> 00:17:07,871
- Put it on my tab.
- You ain't got no tab.

238
00:17:08,040 --> 00:17:10,315
So start me a tab.
I don't work with Peters anymore.

239
00:17:10,480 --> 00:17:11,469
This guy--

240
00:17:11,640 --> 00:17:12,629
When I worked with Joe,

241
00:17:12,800 --> 00:17:15,553
he made me pay cash for everything
in case something happened.

242
00:17:15,720 --> 00:17:17,711
Isn't that right?
Do you remember, you?

243
00:17:19,040 --> 00:17:20,189
Detective Danello?

244
00:17:21,480 --> 00:17:23,755
That's me. What can I do you for?

245
00:17:23,920 --> 00:17:27,469
I work with Ben Matlock.
They said I could find you here.

246
00:17:27,640 --> 00:17:29,995
Yeah, well, they were right.

247
00:17:31,840 --> 00:17:36,356
- I need to talk with you.
- My pleasure. Shall we take a table?

248
00:17:41,920 --> 00:17:43,512
Wish me luck.

249
00:17:44,920 --> 00:17:49,198
- Can I get you a drink?
- No, thank you.

250
00:17:49,760 --> 00:17:53,912
Some guys...
Some guys get all the breaks.

251
00:17:54,080 --> 00:17:56,674
Joe's even got a beautiful attorney.

252
00:17:57,440 --> 00:18:00,830
- You were a good friend to Joe?
- Yeah. Better than he deserved.

253
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:02,513
- How's that?
- I'll tell you, darling.

254
00:18:02,680 --> 00:18:05,319
The life expectancy for Joe's partners
was about two years.

255
00:18:05,480 --> 00:18:08,392
By then, they either got killed
or quit the force.

256
00:18:08,560 --> 00:18:11,313
Joe is not exactly
what you call ''a rabbit's foot.''

257
00:18:11,480 --> 00:18:13,436
I see.

258
00:18:13,600 --> 00:18:15,716
You said he was on that stakeout
with you.

259
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:19,589
He needed an alibi.
That's what partners do, they...

260
00:18:19,760 --> 00:18:23,196
Whether they love each other or not.
You got any more questions?

261
00:18:23,360 --> 00:18:24,349
Because if not,

262
00:18:24,520 --> 00:18:27,114
we could have dinner
at a place a lot nicer than this.

263
00:18:27,640 --> 00:18:29,631
- Detective Danello--
- Call me Mike.

264
00:18:30,960 --> 00:18:32,393
According to the police-radio log,

265
00:18:32,560 --> 00:18:35,028
it took seven minutes
from the time you answered the call

266
00:18:35,200 --> 00:18:36,918
to get to Harry Landers' warehouse.

267
00:18:37,080 --> 00:18:38,513
So?

268
00:18:38,680 --> 00:18:41,319
You reported in from Center and 1 1th,
and it takes 20 minutes

269
00:18:41,720 --> 00:18:43,312
to get from there
to Landers' warehouse.

270
00:18:43,480 --> 00:18:44,549
You're wrong.

271
00:18:44,720 --> 00:18:47,996
No, I'm not. I drove it myself.

272
00:18:48,160 --> 00:18:53,188
- Well, I was in a police car.
- Yes, but it was an unmarked car.

273
00:18:53,360 --> 00:18:55,590
And again, according to the log,
you responded Code 2,

274
00:18:55,760 --> 00:18:58,149
which means that you weren't using
your lights or your siren

275
00:18:58,320 --> 00:19:00,151
and you should've been
obeying the speed limit.

276
00:19:00,320 --> 00:19:04,632
- So maybe I went a little too fast.
- Maybe.

277
00:19:10,560 --> 00:19:14,917
- What's this, a speeding ticket?
- No. It's your subpoena.

278
00:19:16,200 --> 00:19:19,112
I'll see you in court.

279
00:19:42,960 --> 00:19:44,473
Do you mind?

280
00:19:46,120 --> 00:19:47,394
Yes, I do.

281
00:19:49,280 --> 00:19:50,918
You don't like me, do you, friend?

282
00:19:51,080 --> 00:19:52,672
Let's just say
you played it kind of rough

283
00:19:52,840 --> 00:19:54,193
with a few of my buddies.

284
00:20:02,080 --> 00:20:03,274
That's them.

285
00:20:03,720 --> 00:20:05,950
- Hey, just wait a minute.
- Let's go.

286
00:20:06,120 --> 00:20:09,317
Hey, hey, hey.

287
00:20:18,440 --> 00:20:20,078
Come on.

288
00:20:20,480 --> 00:20:22,550
Stop. Police.

289
00:20:25,480 --> 00:20:26,469
Hey.

290
00:20:28,920 --> 00:20:29,955
Get out.

291
00:20:48,240 --> 00:20:50,310
- My leg.
- Just lay still.

292
00:20:50,480 --> 00:20:53,074
Just-- Joe. Hold still.

293
00:21:02,440 --> 00:21:05,750
<i>Dr. Klein. Paging Dr. Klein.</i>

294
00:21:09,640 --> 00:21:14,191
<i>Dr. Caro. Surgery, please. Dr. Caro.</i>

295
00:21:14,640 --> 00:21:16,232
Ma'am.

296
00:21:21,320 --> 00:21:24,710
Joe, how are you?

297
00:21:24,880 --> 00:21:26,871
Terrific.

298
00:21:28,960 --> 00:21:30,996
Thanks. I'm all right.

299
00:21:31,160 --> 00:21:35,438
- Well, that's good to hear.
- Why shouldn't I be?

300
00:21:35,600 --> 00:21:38,319
I've got a broken leg
and I'm being railroaded for murder.

301
00:21:38,480 --> 00:21:42,109
We ran the license number on that car
through the DMV.

302
00:21:42,280 --> 00:21:45,397
- Do you know a Donald Styles?
- No.

303
00:21:45,560 --> 00:21:48,757
Tyler's tracking down the address
on his registration.

304
00:21:48,920 --> 00:21:52,151
- Lots of luck.
- We'll see.

305
00:21:52,640 --> 00:21:56,997
- Your partner, Mike Danello?
- What about him?

306
00:21:57,160 --> 00:21:58,434
His alibi for the Landers killing

307
00:21:58,600 --> 00:22:01,034
was as phoney
as the one he gave you.

308
00:22:01,200 --> 00:22:03,760
He wasn't at that surveillance, either.

309
00:22:04,200 --> 00:22:07,237
- I know.
- Where was he?

310
00:22:07,400 --> 00:22:09,391
Probably with some bimbo.

311
00:22:14,200 --> 00:22:15,918
Your doctor says
you won't be up and about

312
00:22:16,080 --> 00:22:17,672
for another month.

313
00:22:17,840 --> 00:22:20,832
- That's what I hear.
- We'll have your trial continued.

314
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:25,039
- No. You finish it now.
- Joe, you have a right to be there.

315
00:22:25,200 --> 00:22:26,758
Listen, just do me a favour.

316
00:22:26,920 --> 00:22:29,639
However it turns out,
just get it over with.

317
00:22:29,800 --> 00:22:31,995
For God's sake, finish it.

318
00:23:09,560 --> 00:23:12,074
Sorry to bother you, ma'am,
but I'm looking for a Donald Styles.

319
00:23:12,600 --> 00:23:16,912
- Are you the police?
- No, I'm an old friend of his.

320
00:23:17,080 --> 00:23:20,038
There's nobody by that name.
I'm here all alone.

321
00:23:20,200 --> 00:23:23,078
Go away or I'll call the cops.

322
00:23:35,600 --> 00:23:37,352
As I approached the building,

323
00:23:37,520 --> 00:23:40,478
I heard what sounded to me
like a gunshot.

324
00:23:40,640 --> 00:23:41,629
Then what happened?

325
00:23:41,800 --> 00:23:44,075
Well, then the side door
of the warehouse flung open

326
00:23:44,240 --> 00:23:45,753
and this man came running out.

327
00:23:45,920 --> 00:23:47,319
Well, did you recognise him?

328
00:23:47,480 --> 00:23:51,109
Yes, sir, I did.
It was Detective Joseph Peters.

329
00:23:51,800 --> 00:23:53,995
- Are you certain?
- Oh, yes, sir.

330
00:23:54,160 --> 00:23:57,596
I recognized him from the day before,
when he attacked Mr. Landers.

331
00:23:57,760 --> 00:24:00,558
There's no doubt about it. It was him.

332
00:24:00,720 --> 00:24:04,395
Thank you.
Nothing further, Your Honour.

333
00:24:06,800 --> 00:24:09,678
Mr. Coyle, how long had you worked
at the warehouse

334
00:24:09,840 --> 00:24:11,478
before Mr. Landers was killed?

335
00:24:11,640 --> 00:24:12,959
Four days.

336
00:24:13,120 --> 00:24:15,953
And how did you obtain this position
in the first place?

337
00:24:16,120 --> 00:24:18,714
Well, I saw it in an ad
in the newspaper.

338
00:24:18,880 --> 00:24:20,552
Had you ever done
this kind of work before?

339
00:24:20,720 --> 00:24:23,075
- No.
- Did you carry a gun on the job?

340
00:24:23,520 --> 00:24:24,555
Yes.

341
00:24:26,440 --> 00:24:30,115
Mr. Coyle, this is an application

342
00:24:30,280 --> 00:24:34,831
to become a bonded security guard
carrying a gun in this state.

343
00:24:35,720 --> 00:24:37,233
Now, it's my understanding

344
00:24:37,400 --> 00:24:40,551
it takes 90 days
to become permanently bonded.

345
00:24:40,720 --> 00:24:42,711
Well, that's right,
but you can start working

346
00:24:42,880 --> 00:24:45,269
as soon as you finish
filling out the application.

347
00:24:47,920 --> 00:24:50,593
Well, tell me this, Mr. Coyle.

348
00:24:50,760 --> 00:24:53,354
Have you ever been convicted
of a felony?

349
00:24:54,640 --> 00:24:55,868
Yes.

350
00:24:56,040 --> 00:24:59,271
And isn't it true
that you've had over 30 arrests?

351
00:24:59,440 --> 00:25:02,637
- Objection. Improper questioning.
- Sustained.

352
00:25:02,800 --> 00:25:04,438
But the felony,

353
00:25:04,600 --> 00:25:07,239
that was a conviction
for armed robbery, wasn't it?

354
00:25:07,760 --> 00:25:09,159
Yes.

355
00:25:09,320 --> 00:25:12,392
Mr. Coyle, it states very clearly
on this application

356
00:25:12,560 --> 00:25:15,028
that you cannot have
a felony conviction

357
00:25:15,200 --> 00:25:18,237
and become a bonded security guard
in this state.

358
00:25:18,400 --> 00:25:21,233
- Were you aware of that?
- No.

359
00:25:21,400 --> 00:25:24,073
Well, didn't you read the application
before you signed it?

360
00:25:24,960 --> 00:25:29,670
- Yes, but maybe I missed that part.
- Or maybe you're lying.

361
00:25:31,320 --> 00:25:34,517
It seems to me you never intended
to be a security guard very long.

362
00:25:34,680 --> 00:25:36,511
Maybe four days was enough,

363
00:25:36,680 --> 00:25:39,148
just enough to bear false witness
in the Harry Landers murder.

364
00:25:39,320 --> 00:25:42,949
- Objection.
- No further questions, Your Honour.

365
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:49,754
- Thanks for coming, Frank.
- A free lunch? Why not?

366
00:25:51,320 --> 00:25:53,675
I had Tom Coyle on the stand.

367
00:25:53,840 --> 00:25:55,239
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

368
00:25:55,400 --> 00:26:01,077
He's had 32 arrests,
all nickel-and-dime stuff, but arrests.

369
00:26:01,240 --> 00:26:03,674
One conviction.

370
00:26:03,840 --> 00:26:06,559
He's an informant.
That's how he keeps getting off.

371
00:26:06,720 --> 00:26:08,836
He's working for somebody
in your department.

372
00:26:12,640 --> 00:26:15,916
- Someone on my police department?
- Yep.

373
00:26:16,280 --> 00:26:18,350
Well, I find that just a little hard
to believe, Ben.

374
00:26:18,520 --> 00:26:20,829
Sure looks like it.
I need to know who.

375
00:26:21,280 --> 00:26:23,396
Damn, Ben.

376
00:26:25,080 --> 00:26:28,038
And if somebody on the department
is doing something illegal

377
00:26:28,200 --> 00:26:31,590
and got that kind of an informant,
you don't go into the files and get it.

378
00:26:31,760 --> 00:26:36,356
- I mean, he'd keep it to himself.
- Ain't nothing easy, Frank.

379
00:26:40,120 --> 00:26:42,350
Now, you and I go back a long ways.

380
00:26:42,520 --> 00:26:45,318
And all either of us ever wanted
was the truth.

381
00:26:45,480 --> 00:26:47,311
Without it,
Joe Peters is gonna be convicted

382
00:26:47,480 --> 00:26:49,198
of a murder he didn't commit.

383
00:26:49,360 --> 00:26:52,830
Now, somebody in the department
was tipping off Harry Landers,

384
00:26:53,000 --> 00:26:54,911
and that same somebody

385
00:26:55,080 --> 00:26:57,799
got Tom Coyle
to point the finger at Joe.

386
00:26:58,920 --> 00:27:00,831
Yeah,
but what you're asking me to do--

387
00:27:01,000 --> 00:27:02,911
I mean,
that puts me in a bad spot, Ben.

388
00:27:03,080 --> 00:27:05,230
I know it does, but you arrested him.

389
00:27:05,400 --> 00:27:07,470
You've got a stake in this
whether you like it or not.

390
00:27:07,640 --> 00:27:09,392
Oh, come on,
I'd rather take a beating.

391
00:27:09,560 --> 00:27:11,596
The truth, Frank, the truth.

392
00:27:11,760 --> 00:27:15,150
Without it, Joe's out of luck
and so am I and so are you.

393
00:27:19,040 --> 00:27:22,430
Ben, I've been a cop for 23 years,
and I have never--

394
00:27:22,600 --> 00:27:23,589
I have never.

395
00:27:23,760 --> 00:27:25,910
--spied on my brother officer.

396
00:27:26,080 --> 00:27:28,230
All I'm asking is you look into it.

397
00:27:28,400 --> 00:27:30,152
Then if you don't think
there's a connection,

398
00:27:30,320 --> 00:27:33,278
I'll forget the whole thing,
and you're off the hook.

399
00:27:38,280 --> 00:27:40,840
Yeah, thanks, Ben.

400
00:27:41,320 --> 00:27:45,552
I show you this police revolver
marked ''People's Exhibit 7.''

401
00:27:45,720 --> 00:27:49,190
- Can you identify it?
- Yes, sir. It has my initials.

402
00:27:50,440 --> 00:27:51,509
Would you...?

403
00:27:51,680 --> 00:27:54,433
Would you tell the court
where you found it?

404
00:27:54,600 --> 00:27:55,589
On a ledge in a sewer

405
00:27:55,760 --> 00:27:59,036
three blocks west
of Harry Landers' warehouse.

406
00:27:59,880 --> 00:28:04,032
Had it not dropped on the ledge,
had it fallen all the way into the sewer,

407
00:28:04,200 --> 00:28:06,919
what would've become of this gun?

408
00:28:07,080 --> 00:28:09,913
I think it's safe to say
it never would've been found.

409
00:28:11,240 --> 00:28:12,229
As part of your duties,

410
00:28:12,400 --> 00:28:15,073
did you have a ballistics test performed
on this weapon?

411
00:28:15,240 --> 00:28:17,879
- Yes, sir, I did.
- And what were the results?

412
00:28:18,040 --> 00:28:19,792
Bullets taken from the deceased

413
00:28:19,960 --> 00:28:22,315
and those fired
in laboratory tests of this weapon

414
00:28:22,480 --> 00:28:25,472
showed a significant number
of points of comparison.

415
00:28:28,800 --> 00:28:29,835
In your opinion,

416
00:28:31,320 --> 00:28:33,117
it was the murder weapon, correct?

417
00:28:33,280 --> 00:28:35,236
In my opinion, yes, sir.

418
00:28:35,720 --> 00:28:38,598
As requested,
did you bring with you today

419
00:28:39,120 --> 00:28:41,588
the departmental records
reflecting the ownership

420
00:28:41,760 --> 00:28:44,718
and the registration
of Officer Peters' service revolvers?

421
00:28:44,880 --> 00:28:46,393
- Yes, sir, I did.
- And?

422
00:28:47,000 --> 00:28:50,072
The weapon is registered
to Detective Joseph Peters.

423
00:28:52,040 --> 00:28:55,953
- No further questions, Your Honour.
- Cross-examine.

424
00:29:02,680 --> 00:29:05,911
Officer Price, would you characterise
the decedent and Detective Peters

425
00:29:06,080 --> 00:29:08,230
as friends or as enemies?

426
00:29:08,400 --> 00:29:11,073
- As enemies.
- I see.

427
00:29:11,240 --> 00:29:14,630
Did you participate in the search
of the premises after the murder?

428
00:29:14,800 --> 00:29:15,869
Yes, ma'am, I did.

429
00:29:16,040 --> 00:29:17,871
Would you mind telling the court
what you found

430
00:29:18,040 --> 00:29:20,270
in the upper right-hand drawer
of Mr. Landers' desk?

431
00:29:20,440 --> 00:29:23,159
A .357 Magnum revolver.

432
00:29:23,320 --> 00:29:26,471
Now, if Mr. Landers
and Detective Peters were enemies,

433
00:29:26,640 --> 00:29:29,871
as you say, don't you find it strange

434
00:29:30,040 --> 00:29:32,713
that Mr. Landers
didn't take out his gun?

435
00:29:32,880 --> 00:29:34,791
Unless, of course,
it was somebody else

436
00:29:34,960 --> 00:29:37,269
that Harry Landers
let into his office that day,

437
00:29:37,440 --> 00:29:39,795
somebody Landers thought
was a friend.

438
00:29:39,960 --> 00:29:41,552
And that's why
he never took out his gun.

439
00:29:41,720 --> 00:29:45,030
- Objection.
- No further questions, Your Honour.

440
00:29:56,640 --> 00:29:57,629
What is it?

441
00:29:57,800 --> 00:29:59,552
Have you seen Frank Daniels
anywhere?

442
00:29:59,720 --> 00:30:01,199
No. Why?

443
00:30:01,360 --> 00:30:04,909
Well, I was hoping he'd come through
with a little inside information.

444
00:30:05,080 --> 00:30:09,119
- You think he will?
- I don't know. It is pretty hard on him.

445
00:30:10,240 --> 00:30:12,708
- Well, I'm going to lunch.
- I'd better hang around here.

446
00:30:12,880 --> 00:30:15,394
- All right, I have some errands to do.
- Charlene?

447
00:30:17,160 --> 00:30:18,957
Could you lend me out a five?

448
00:30:20,880 --> 00:30:22,950
I left my money in my other suit.

449
00:30:24,800 --> 00:30:26,119
What other suit?

450
00:30:28,240 --> 00:30:31,869
- Could you lend me out a five?
- Okay.

451
00:30:32,960 --> 00:30:35,474
Let's see. What have we got?

452
00:30:35,640 --> 00:30:40,794
One, two, three...
That's four. Here's five.

453
00:30:40,960 --> 00:30:44,077
- Now, stay away from the hot dogs.
- Yeah.

454
00:30:45,280 --> 00:30:47,191
- Ben, there's a phone call for you.
- Thank you.

455
00:30:47,360 --> 00:30:50,636
Thanks for the--
And soon as-- Soon as I...

456
00:30:54,640 --> 00:30:56,949
- Ben Matlock.
<i>- Yeah, Ben, it's Tyler.</i>

457
00:30:57,120 --> 00:30:59,395
I went to the address
on Donny Styles' registration.

458
00:30:59,560 --> 00:31:01,630
There's nobody there
but an old lady in a wheelchair,

459
00:31:01,800 --> 00:31:02,869
says she lives alone.

460
00:31:03,040 --> 00:31:05,793
But I did spot some fresh oil
in the driveway.

461
00:31:05,960 --> 00:31:08,155
- Any sign of his car?
- Guess what.

462
00:31:08,320 --> 00:31:12,279
About ten minutes ago, he pulled up,
parked it in the garage.

463
00:31:13,040 --> 00:31:15,838
Good work, Tyler.
Keep an eye on him.

464
00:31:45,360 --> 00:31:47,635
I didn't have any breakfast.

465
00:31:51,120 --> 00:31:52,951
Hello, Frank.

466
00:32:27,240 --> 00:32:29,834
- Oh, evening, counsellor.
- Evening.

467
00:32:31,320 --> 00:32:35,029
You know,
the more I get into this case,

468
00:32:35,200 --> 00:32:38,556
the more certain I am
that Harry Landers had an informant

469
00:32:38,720 --> 00:32:40,551
inside the department.

470
00:32:41,280 --> 00:32:43,271
What's that gonna do for your client?

471
00:32:43,440 --> 00:32:47,274
Well, with a little bit of luck
and an intelligent jury,

472
00:32:47,440 --> 00:32:48,759
I think it's gonna clear him.

473
00:32:51,160 --> 00:32:54,789
See, Joe Peters
wasn't the inside man.

474
00:32:54,960 --> 00:32:56,951
- You were.
- I was?

475
00:32:57,120 --> 00:32:58,838
See, when Joe started getting close,

476
00:32:59,000 --> 00:33:01,195
you had to shut things down
pretty fast,

477
00:33:01,360 --> 00:33:03,430
so you planted your man Tom Coyle.

478
00:33:03,600 --> 00:33:06,910
Then you either killed Harry Landers
or you had him killed,

479
00:33:07,080 --> 00:33:10,277
and Tom Coyle was right there
to hang the murder on Joe.

480
00:33:12,080 --> 00:33:14,435
You don't think
I can convince the jury of this, do you?

481
00:33:14,600 --> 00:33:18,229
- No.
- Come see for yourself.

482
00:33:18,400 --> 00:33:21,790
This subpoena guarantees you
the best seat in the house.

483
00:33:22,400 --> 00:33:24,595
I wouldn't miss it for the world.

484
00:33:47,440 --> 00:33:50,477
Donny, it's time we had a little talk.

485
00:33:57,560 --> 00:34:00,472
- Morning, Donny.
- Who are you?

486
00:34:00,640 --> 00:34:03,154
I'm Joe Peters' lawyer.

487
00:34:03,320 --> 00:34:07,359
- Well, what do you want from me?
- I wanna help you.

488
00:34:08,200 --> 00:34:09,189
Help me, huh?

489
00:34:09,360 --> 00:34:11,749
Help you keep from getting in
any deeper, Donny.

490
00:34:13,000 --> 00:34:15,070
I don't know
what you're talking about.

491
00:34:15,240 --> 00:34:17,629
We're talking about murder.

492
00:34:17,800 --> 00:34:20,712
Who sent you
to steal Joe Peters' gun?

493
00:34:20,880 --> 00:34:23,189
I didn't steal any gun.

494
00:34:24,720 --> 00:34:29,669
Donny, let's play a ''let's say'' game.

495
00:34:29,840 --> 00:34:33,549
Let's say that I'm somebody,
maybe a cop,

496
00:34:33,720 --> 00:34:36,029
and I wanna
get rid of a couple of guys.

497
00:34:36,200 --> 00:34:38,316
I wanna kill Harry Landers

498
00:34:38,480 --> 00:34:41,438
and I want Joe Peters
to get the blame for it.

499
00:34:41,600 --> 00:34:44,239
Now, what do you think
would be a good move for me?

500
00:34:45,000 --> 00:34:46,956
I don't know. Why don't you tell me?

501
00:34:47,760 --> 00:34:49,716
Well, how about this?

502
00:34:49,880 --> 00:34:52,075
How about I hire a couple of kids,

503
00:34:52,240 --> 00:34:55,630
and one of them
is a pretty good pickpocket?

504
00:34:55,800 --> 00:34:59,315
And I hired this kid
to steal Joe Peters' gun.

505
00:34:59,920 --> 00:35:01,558
While he's at it,
he takes his badge too,

506
00:35:01,720 --> 00:35:02,709
but that's okay.

507
00:35:02,880 --> 00:35:04,199
Now, I don't tell the kid

508
00:35:04,360 --> 00:35:05,918
that the gun's gonna be used
for murder.

509
00:35:06,080 --> 00:35:09,277
He might not like that.
He just gets the gun.

510
00:35:09,440 --> 00:35:11,317
Then later, if he wants to holler,

511
00:35:11,480 --> 00:35:15,393
I can get rid of the kid any time,
one way or another.

512
00:35:18,280 --> 00:35:21,317
The gun you stole
was used to kill Harry Landers.

513
00:35:21,480 --> 00:35:23,311
You're an accessory to murder,
Donny.

514
00:35:23,480 --> 00:35:25,038
And like they used to say
in the movies,

515
00:35:25,200 --> 00:35:26,713
that buys the big ticket.

516
00:35:27,160 --> 00:35:31,073
Now, unless you cooperate,
it's just gonna get worse.

517
00:35:33,560 --> 00:35:37,235
- Get out of my way.
- Here.

518
00:35:37,400 --> 00:35:40,358
My number's on that. Call any time.

519
00:35:42,760 --> 00:35:47,038
- That's the last we'll see of him.
- Maybe.

520
00:36:07,040 --> 00:36:09,873
Okay, I'm here. What's the problem?

521
00:36:10,040 --> 00:36:13,396
That cop's lawyer,
he came and saw me yesterday.

522
00:36:13,560 --> 00:36:15,152
He knows who we are.

523
00:36:15,320 --> 00:36:18,551
Correction:
He knows who you are, Donny.

524
00:36:18,720 --> 00:36:20,392
You didn't give him anything else,
did you?

525
00:36:21,040 --> 00:36:22,359
Now, you look.

526
00:36:22,520 --> 00:36:25,114
I shined him on,
but you gotta get him off of me.

527
00:36:26,080 --> 00:36:28,640
Now, he says
that I could be an accessory.

528
00:36:30,480 --> 00:36:32,835
Now, I said I would take care of you,
and I will.

529
00:36:33,000 --> 00:36:34,228
Don't worry.

530
00:36:34,400 --> 00:36:36,516
But you futz around with me, boy,

531
00:36:36,680 --> 00:36:39,399
and there's places I can lose you
as easy as a paper clip.

532
00:36:39,560 --> 00:36:42,199
Now, I got guys on the inside
who owe me favours.

533
00:36:42,360 --> 00:36:44,669
You'd be worth maybe-- Maybe.
--a pack of cigarettes.

534
00:36:44,840 --> 00:36:46,068
Now, you got that?

535
00:36:46,240 --> 00:36:50,119
Yeah. Right.
Right, anything you say.

536
00:36:50,280 --> 00:36:54,239
Fine. Fine.

537
00:36:54,760 --> 00:36:57,194
Everything's gonna be fine.

538
00:36:57,360 --> 00:36:59,396
We're gonna look back on this
and we're gonna laugh,

539
00:36:59,560 --> 00:37:00,549
I promise you.

540
00:37:02,720 --> 00:37:04,551
Just to be on the safe side,

541
00:37:04,720 --> 00:37:06,790
I got something I want you to do,
Eddie, okay?

542
00:37:06,960 --> 00:37:10,953
Absolutely, Mr. B. You bet.

543
00:37:14,360 --> 00:37:16,271
Captain Braddock,

544
00:37:17,080 --> 00:37:20,834
for the last 1 8 months,
you've headed a task force

545
00:37:21,000 --> 00:37:25,039
investigating the criminal activities
of Mr. Harry Landers, have you not?

546
00:37:25,200 --> 00:37:26,189
Yes.

547
00:37:26,360 --> 00:37:28,635
Mr. Landers is reputed to be a fence,

548
00:37:28,800 --> 00:37:31,234
that is, a receiver and dealer
in stolen goods.

549
00:37:31,400 --> 00:37:33,630
- Is that correct?
- Yes.

550
00:37:33,800 --> 00:37:35,438
As a result of your investigations,

551
00:37:35,600 --> 00:37:37,556
did you determine
that Mr. Landers dealt

552
00:37:37,720 --> 00:37:40,234
in thousands of dollars of materials

553
00:37:40,400 --> 00:37:43,631
or hundreds of thousands
or in the millions?

554
00:37:44,200 --> 00:37:47,875
- Probably in the millions.
- A large operation, in other words.

555
00:37:48,720 --> 00:37:50,278
Where did he keep
all this merchandise?

556
00:37:50,960 --> 00:37:54,953
In various places,
warehouses around the city.

557
00:37:55,120 --> 00:37:57,918
Did you ever
raid these various places?

558
00:37:58,080 --> 00:37:59,069
Oh, yes.

559
00:37:59,240 --> 00:38:00,639
According to departmental records,

560
00:38:00,800 --> 00:38:03,268
27 separate raids
on these warehouses.

561
00:38:03,440 --> 00:38:05,351
Does that sound about right to you?

562
00:38:05,800 --> 00:38:08,712
I don't remember the exact number,
but that sounds right.

563
00:38:09,280 --> 00:38:10,599
As a result of these raids,

564
00:38:10,760 --> 00:38:15,629
were you able to obtain an arrest
and conviction of Mr. Landers?

565
00:38:16,400 --> 00:38:17,549
Never.

566
00:38:17,720 --> 00:38:20,837
- Not even once?
- No.

567
00:38:21,320 --> 00:38:22,958
That's remarkable.

568
00:38:23,120 --> 00:38:25,680
One might assume
that he knew when you were coming.

569
00:38:27,200 --> 00:38:28,792
Yes, sir.

570
00:38:28,960 --> 00:38:32,839
It's my opinion that Detective Peters
was tipping Mr. Landers off.

571
00:38:33,000 --> 00:38:35,833
Objection. Highly improper.
Move to strike.

572
00:38:36,000 --> 00:38:39,549
Granted.
The statement shall be stricken.

573
00:38:39,720 --> 00:38:42,712
Captain Braddock,
you've been in the witness box before.

574
00:38:42,880 --> 00:38:43,949
You know the game.

575
00:38:44,120 --> 00:38:47,510
I ask the questions,
you answer just my questions.

576
00:38:47,680 --> 00:38:48,999
No opinions. No speculations.

577
00:38:49,160 --> 00:38:51,549
- Do we understand each other?
- Objection.

578
00:38:51,720 --> 00:38:54,359
Mr. Matlock
is harassing his own witness.

579
00:38:54,520 --> 00:38:57,512
I apologise to the court
and withdraw the last question.

580
00:38:57,680 --> 00:38:59,113
Mr. Braddock,

581
00:38:59,280 --> 00:39:03,034
before these raids happened,
who knew the time and place?

582
00:39:04,360 --> 00:39:06,999
Peters always knew.

583
00:39:07,160 --> 00:39:09,469
As head of the task force,
you must have known.

584
00:39:11,040 --> 00:39:13,554
- Yes.
- And who else?

585
00:39:13,720 --> 00:39:16,029
The judge who signed the warrant,
the clerk of his court,

586
00:39:16,200 --> 00:39:19,397
backup personnel, watch commander,
desk sergeant, motor-pool officers.

587
00:39:19,560 --> 00:39:20,913
Did I leave out anybody?

588
00:39:25,320 --> 00:39:28,278
<i>Dr. Warner wanted in Radiology,</i>
<i>please.</i>

589
00:39:28,440 --> 00:39:30,510
<i>Dr. Warner.</i>

590
00:39:47,360 --> 00:39:50,636
<i>Dr. Klein. Paging Dr. Klein.</i>

591
00:39:55,320 --> 00:39:56,833
Captain Braddock,

592
00:39:57,000 --> 00:39:59,833
the most telling evidence
against Detective Peters

593
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:02,560
is that his gun
has been positively identified

594
00:40:02,720 --> 00:40:04,392
as the murder weapon.

595
00:40:04,560 --> 00:40:07,916
But defence contends
that that gun was stolen

596
00:40:08,080 --> 00:40:11,231
24 hours
before the murder took place.

597
00:40:11,400 --> 00:40:14,392
Yes, sir.
I'm aware that is your contention.

598
00:40:14,560 --> 00:40:18,678
Now, Detective Peters' badge
was also stolen at the same time,

599
00:40:18,840 --> 00:40:21,035
we assume by the same people.

600
00:40:21,560 --> 00:40:24,393
The gun's been found by officers
working under your supervision,

601
00:40:24,560 --> 00:40:25,879
but the shield is still missing.

602
00:40:26,040 --> 00:40:29,112
- Where do you suppose it is?
- I have no idea.

603
00:40:29,280 --> 00:40:32,477
Whoever stole that gun
or had it stolen

604
00:40:32,640 --> 00:40:35,473
is likely responsible
for Harry Landers' murder.

605
00:40:36,720 --> 00:40:41,191
- If your contention is correct.
- If our contention is correct.

606
00:40:41,360 --> 00:40:43,271
Now, let me make it clear.

607
00:40:43,440 --> 00:40:47,877
Detective Peters' badge
was also stolen at the same time.

608
00:40:48,040 --> 00:40:49,996
Now, you will agree.

609
00:40:50,560 --> 00:40:53,393
If we knew who has that badge,

610
00:40:53,560 --> 00:40:59,032
it would go a long ways
to support defence's claim.

611
00:40:59,800 --> 00:41:03,315
Well, I suppose theoretically, yes.

612
00:41:05,160 --> 00:41:07,594
Would Mr. Donny Styles
please stand?

613
00:41:13,120 --> 00:41:15,270
Do you recognise this man?

614
00:41:16,480 --> 00:41:17,515
No.

615
00:41:19,120 --> 00:41:20,599
You've never seen him before?

616
00:41:20,760 --> 00:41:22,273
- No.
- Objection, Your Honour.

617
00:41:22,440 --> 00:41:26,149
- Question was asked and answered.
- Sustained.

618
00:41:26,320 --> 00:41:29,517
Captain Braddock,
this young man says he knows you.

619
00:41:32,280 --> 00:41:33,998
He stepped forward this morning

620
00:41:34,160 --> 00:41:37,152
and made a deposition under oath
that he and a friend

621
00:41:37,320 --> 00:41:40,949
stole Detective Peters' gun
at your instructions

622
00:41:41,120 --> 00:41:43,156
and in the process
took his badge as well.

623
00:41:43,320 --> 00:41:44,958
That is a complete fabrication.

624
00:41:45,120 --> 00:41:46,678
Objection. If defence has a witness,

625
00:41:46,840 --> 00:41:48,558
let's swear him in
and put him on the stand.

626
00:41:48,720 --> 00:41:49,994
- Otherwise--
- Mr. Prosecutor,

627
00:41:50,160 --> 00:41:52,628
I intend to do just that
if it becomes necessary.

628
00:41:52,800 --> 00:41:55,553
But right now I would like
to continue my examination

629
00:41:55,720 --> 00:41:57,358
of the witness already on the stand.

630
00:41:57,520 --> 00:42:00,318
- Proceed, counsellor.
- Thank you, Your Honour.

631
00:42:00,480 --> 00:42:03,870
Captain Braddock,
isn't it a departmental rule

632
00:42:04,040 --> 00:42:06,600
that Atlanta policemen
must carry their shields at all times?

633
00:42:07,480 --> 00:42:08,754
Yes.

634
00:42:08,920 --> 00:42:12,117
- Do you have yours with you now?
- Yes.

635
00:42:12,280 --> 00:42:13,998
May I take a look at it, please?

636
00:42:17,720 --> 00:42:20,917
Don't hand it to me.
Just hold it up so I can look at it.

637
00:42:24,960 --> 00:42:27,554
- What's the number?
- Eight-three-oh.

638
00:42:27,720 --> 00:42:30,234
- Are you sure?
- Yes, I'm sure.

639
00:42:30,760 --> 00:42:32,671
That's interesting.

640
00:42:33,480 --> 00:42:36,040
It doesn't say 830.

641
00:42:36,200 --> 00:42:39,158
This is a detective's badge, 7 7 1 .

642
00:42:40,560 --> 00:42:42,835
That's Joe Peters' badge.

643
00:42:43,560 --> 00:42:44,959
Your Honour,

644
00:42:45,120 --> 00:42:48,476
we'd like to offer this badge
as Defendant's Exhibit G.

645
00:42:49,240 --> 00:42:51,231
Captain Braddock,

646
00:42:51,400 --> 00:42:54,119
how did you come
to be in possession of this badge?

647
00:42:55,440 --> 00:42:57,158
Then I'll tell you.

648
00:42:57,840 --> 00:43:00,400
Donny Styles
is an expert pickpocket.

649
00:43:00,560 --> 00:43:02,551
When you met with him
and Eddie Leeds this morning,

650
00:43:02,720 --> 00:43:05,075
he bumped you, and in so doing,

651
00:43:05,240 --> 00:43:10,155
he switched your badge
and holder for Joe Peters'.

652
00:43:10,320 --> 00:43:12,470
You're the one
Harry Landers was paying off.

653
00:43:12,640 --> 00:43:14,358
No, sir. Absolutely not.

654
00:43:14,520 --> 00:43:17,557
He threatened to expose you
unless you got Joe Peters off his back.

655
00:43:17,720 --> 00:43:18,948
That's not true.

656
00:43:19,120 --> 00:43:21,350
So you hired Donny Styles
and Eddie Leeds

657
00:43:21,520 --> 00:43:22,839
to steal Joe Peters' gun.

658
00:43:23,000 --> 00:43:25,594
Then you used that gun
to kill Harry Landers.

659
00:43:25,760 --> 00:43:28,035
These questions are insulting
and defamatory.

660
00:43:28,200 --> 00:43:29,713
And isn't it true,
at this very moment,

661
00:43:29,880 --> 00:43:31,632
Eddie Leeds
is at County General Hospital,

662
00:43:31,800 --> 00:43:35,190
sent there by you to kill Joe Peters?

663
00:44:05,240 --> 00:44:06,878
Drop it or I'll break your arm.

664
00:44:11,000 --> 00:44:13,355
<i>If Joe Peters were killed,</i>

665
00:44:13,520 --> 00:44:15,511
there would be
no further investigations

666
00:44:15,680 --> 00:44:17,796
into this matter.

667
00:44:17,960 --> 00:44:19,712
And so Eddie Leeds,

668
00:44:19,880 --> 00:44:22,269
acting on orders
from Captain Braddock,

669
00:44:22,440 --> 00:44:27,798
did in fact try to kill Joe Peters
while he lay helpless in a hospital bed.

670
00:44:27,960 --> 00:44:30,838
What the court decides to do
with Captain Braddock

671
00:44:31,000 --> 00:44:32,035
is out of my hands.

672
00:44:32,200 --> 00:44:35,158
What I'm asking of you,
ladies and gentlemen of the jury,

673
00:44:35,320 --> 00:44:41,111
is that you set Joe Peters,
an innocent man, free of all charges.

674
00:44:41,720 --> 00:44:43,199
Thank you.

675
00:44:44,760 --> 00:44:46,239
Be seated.

676
00:44:54,480 --> 00:44:59,076
- Has the jury reached a verdict?
- Yes, we have, Your Honour.

677
00:44:59,560 --> 00:45:02,677
We find the defendant not guilty.

678
00:45:02,840 --> 00:45:05,035
Court is adjourned.

679
00:45:05,920 --> 00:45:08,309
- I wanna thank you.
- Why don't you?

680
00:45:08,480 --> 00:45:10,994
- Thanks. Thank you.
- Okay.

681
00:45:11,160 --> 00:45:12,434
- Thank you.
- Hey, you know what?

682
00:45:12,600 --> 00:45:14,318
I'm glad I caught you.

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
<font color="#ffff00" size=14>www.tvsubtitles.net</font>
